{"version":1,"content":"<p>韓國科學技術院（KAIST）與首爾大學盆唐醫院的研究團隊開發出一種可穿戴微流控眼藥貼片，目標是在微重力環境下幫助太空人自行滴眼藥。研究發表於《傳感器與執行器B：化學》期刊。NASA指出，微重力會使體液向頭部移動，可能增加眼部壓力並引發視力問題；而普通滴眼液依靠重力落入眼中，在失重環境下不易使用。</p> <a href=\"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/science/1583566.htm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>閲讀全文</strong></a>","scraped_at":"2026-10-23T13:04:42.751296+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":153,"images":0,"source":"cnBeta","fallback":"rss-budget","origin":"rss","completeness":"unverified"},"published_at":"2026-10-23T11:33:43+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-23T12:58:11.861481+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-10-23T12:58:11.861481+00:00","content_hash":"e6e62482c8d75ae86d0848ead8c09d77483bb377b30e1906b7803695ed12c202","evidence_status":"partial","scrape_error":null,"content_retention":null,"content_capture":null}